<% @page_title = "Account management guide" %>
<% client, clients = term(:client).downcase, term(:client, count: 2).downcase %>
<% member = AccountManagement::Member.for(Current.user) %>
<% leads = AccountManagement::Lead.where(user: Current.user) %>

<% if member %>
  <%= render "account_management/nav", current: :guide %>
<% end %>

<div class="panel accounts-panel shadow txt-align-start flex flex-column gap">
  <section class="settings__section">
    <header>
      <h2 class="divider">What it’s for</h2>
    </header>
    <p>Account management keeps every <%= client %> in play. It does five things, one per page in the sidebar:</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Today:</strong> what needs you across your <%= clients %>, most urgent first.</li>
      <li><strong><%= clients.upcase_first %>:</strong> who leads each one, how it’s doing this week, and when it last heard from us. Riskiest first.</li>
      <li><strong>Contacts:</strong> every call, email, text and visit, so a <%= client %> never goes quiet unnoticed.</li>
      <li><strong>Meetings:</strong> an agenda a day ahead, a recap within a day after, action items that become commitments.</li>
      <li><strong>Calls:</strong> your notes from a call, debriefed by AI into work on the right <%= term(:engagement, count: 2).downcase %>, owned by the right people.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="settings__section">
    <header>
      <h2 class="divider">Where you are</h2>
    </header>
    <ol class="record-steps txt-small">
      <li><strong><%= member ? "✓ It’s switched on for you." : "It isn’t switched on for you yet." %></strong> <% unless member %><%= can?(:manage_settings) ? link_to("Switch it on in Settings", account_management_settings_path, class: "txt-link") : "Ask an owner to switch it on." %><% end %></li>
      <% if member %>
        <li><strong>You work with <%= member.all_clients? ? "every #{client}" : pluralize(member.clients.count, client) %>.</strong> <%= link_to "Change in My #{clients}", account_management_portfolio_path, class: "txt-link" %></li>
        <li><strong>You lead <%= pluralize(leads.count, client) %><% if leads.where(backup_user_id: nil).exists? %>, <%= leads.where(backup_user_id: nil).count %> without a backup<% end %>.</strong> Set a backup on each <%= client %>’s Account management tab.</li>
        <li><strong>Start each day on <%= link_to "Today", account_management_root_path, class: "txt-link" %>.</strong></li>
      <% end %>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="settings__section">
    <header>
      <h2 class="divider">Setting it up</h2>
    </header>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>An owner switches it on</strong> for the people who look after <%= clients %> in <%= link_to "the Account management settings", account_management_settings_path, class: "txt-link" %>, and sets what each person on the team does (code, design, seo…), which is how work from a call finds its owner.</li>
      <li><strong>Each <%= client %> gets a lead and a backup</strong> on its Account management tab. <%= clients.upcase_first %> without a lead show up for managers until they have one.</li>
      <li><strong>Each person chooses their <%= clients %></strong> in My <%= clients %>: every one, or a group. The ones they lead or back up are always theirs.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="settings__section">
    <header>
      <h2 class="divider">Every day</h2>
    </header>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Work Today from the top:</strong> Overdue, Today, This week, then Keep an eye on. Each item links to where you act on it. Not ready? <strong>Snooze</strong> it (the bell); it comes back on its own.</li>
      <li><strong>Log every contact.</strong> Press <kbd>a</kbd>, then <strong>Contact</strong>, or use <strong>Log a contact</strong> on the <%= client %>’s tab. Meetings, call and email notes, requests and agreements count on their own; internal notes don’t. A <%= client %> is quiet after <%= AccountManagement::Playbook::CONTACT_EVERY %> days without us, unless its lead sets another cadence.</li>
      <li><strong>Answer requests within <%= pluralize(AccountManagement::Playbook::REPLY_WITHIN, "business day") %>.</strong> A request is answered when it’s triaged, or when you log a contact with that <%= client %> after it came in.</li>
      <li><strong>By the end of Thursday, set each <%= client %>’s health:</strong> on track, at risk or off track, with a line saying why.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="settings__section">
    <header>
      <h2 class="divider">Every meeting</h2>
    </header>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Plan it,</strong> or set a rhythm on the <%= client %>’s tab so the next one is always planned.</li>
      <li><strong>Draft the agenda from the records</strong> (what’s open from last time, what each side owes, decisions we need, what’s coming up), add what the records can’t know, and send it <strong>a day ahead</strong>.</li>
      <li><strong>After it, start the recap from the agenda,</strong> fill in the decisions, add each action item with an owner and a date, and send it <strong>within a day</strong>.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="settings__section">
    <header>
      <h2 class="divider">After every call</h2>
    </header>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Paste your notes into your AI app</strong> (Claude Code with the <code>runwell</code> CLI, or any app connected to Runwell) and say <strong>“debrief this call with &lt;<%= client %>&gt;”</strong>.</li>
      <li><strong>It shows you the plan first:</strong> each todo with its <%= term(:engagement).downcase %>, owner and due date, the commitments, requests for anything outside the agreed scope, and health. Say what to change.</li>
      <li><strong>Then it records the call:</strong> the notes, the contact and every item at once, listed under Calls.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="txt-small txt-subtle">No AI app to hand? The <%= client %>’s tab has <strong>Debrief a call</strong> with <strong>Copy for AI</strong>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="settings__section">
    <header>
      <h2 class="divider">When you’re away</h2>
    </header>
    <p>Set <strong>Away until</strong> in My <%= clients %>. While you’re away, each <%= client %> you lead goes to its backup: their Today, their home warnings.</p>
  </section>
</div>
